From: Mr Douvis <douvis@hellenic-culture-ministry.example> (Ministry of Culture, Organising Committee)
To: Barry Adams <barry.adams@ram-media.example> (RAM Media)
Date: 2006-10-24
Subject: RE: Meeting of 19 October and the third instalment

We refer to the "subjects which were discussed and agreed between us in the meeting of 19th October 2006."

"It is with surprise that we realise complete distortion of what was agreed. We are completely unable to comprehend your behaviour and furthermore completely unable to handle henceforth the case of the Ceremony of the 2006 ... Awards".

1. RAM has not already sent the letter to the National Bank.
2. What was agreed was that the bank, on RAM's application, would send a letter to the Ministry by which the term "good execution" would be extended to include an additional obligation upon RAM to secure the attendance of six (not five) winners, and the expiry date of the letter of guarantee would be extended from 6th to 9th November.
3. There was no agreement on the proposed role for the independent lawyer.
4. The Ministry is not in breach of contract. RAM's omissions have left the Committee unable to realise the sponsorship benefits envisaged, because it cannot give prospective sponsors the number of winning players who will attend, nor the participating artists, presenters and celebrities.

"... we consider that not only technically but also it is a matter of substance it is you who are in ... complete breach of contract, taking also into consideration the numerous affirmative letters of ... [FIFPro] ... (the last one was dated 23 October 2006, nine working days before the gala, that they cannot ensure presence of awarded players in the gala".

Douvis
Organising Committee

--
RECONSTRUCTED FROM THE PUBLISHED JUDGMENT. Not an original document.
Source: RAM Media v Ministry of Culture of the Hellenic Republic [2008] EWHC 1835 (QB), paras 45, 92-93.
Sent as a letter. Points 1-4 are the judge's summary, not the original wording.
